media: i2c: dw9807-vcm: DW9808 compatible, vcc supply, SAC bring-up

The Dongwoon DW9808 is the lens driver of the Galaxy Tab S8+ (SM-X800)
rear camera module. It answers at 7-bit 0x0c on a GENI I2C bus and uses
the DW9807 register map: control at 0x02, the 10-bit position split over
0x03 and 0x04, busy status at 0x05, SAC mode at 0x06 and ring timing at
0x07. The mainline dw9807-vcm driver moves it as is. Two things it
cannot do without help:

1. Power. The lens shares the module rail with the sensor (stock names
   it cam_vaf, 3.3 V, behind the CAM_LDO_EN pin, with the 1.8 V I/O
   LDO behind it). Without a supply of its own the driver can only talk
   to the chip while the sensor streams, and the probe-time runtime
   suspend writes to a dead chip. An optional vcc-supply is enabled on
   runtime resume, with the 10 ms settle stock allows, and disabled on
   runtime suspend. With the supply described, probe leaves the device
   suspended instead of writing power-down to an unpowered chip. System
   sleep goes through pm_runtime_force_suspend and resume so the
   regulator enable count stays balanced.

2. Ringing control. The vendor camera stack brings the DW9808 up with
   control 0x01 then 0x00, a 5 ms settle, mode 0x60, ring timing 0x05,
   a stepped move to the start position and finally control 0x02, which
   turns SAC ringing control on. The new dongwoon,dw9808-vcm compatible
   selects that sequence on resume; the DW9807 path is unchanged apart
   from the shared register write helper.

The values come from the stock SM-X800 CamX actuator module decode
(issue #27) and match the Tab S9 out-of-tree dw9808_vcm.c
(nacht20-de/gts9wifi-fedora), which carries the same 13-write sequence.

Binding: add the compatible and vcc-supply.

